 "minutes": null,
 "description": "Short food-safety spot visit: stock areas, food safety checks, cleaning and hygiene, crew hygiene, pest management and documentation.",
 "instructions": "Total possible points may change with the number of equipment items in use on the day of the audit; use the possible total at the end of each section.\nGrading: 95.0-100 = A, 90.0-94.9 = B, 80.0-89.9 = C, below 80 = F. An item marked critical (a failure shown as “/F” in the source form) makes the whole audit an automatic F.\nAction plan timelines by risk: Low (does not directly affect hygiene or food safety) - by the next audit; Medium (could affect hygiene or food safety) - within 1 month; High (increased food-safety risk) - within 1 week; Critical (unacceptable, affects food safety) - immediately.",
